                "word": "Hamhung",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0a3c31e1-9742-314e-b508-744576bfc315",
                        "entry_id": "722abc0d-f94a-381c-9bc0-99cc7796e691",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The provincial capital of South Hamgyong Province, North Korea; the country's 2nd-largest city and 3rd-largest port."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "91c2626a-d9d3-4d06-815c-4942d0b18739",
                                "sense_id": "0a3c31e1-9742-314e-b508-744576bfc315",
                                "text": "Author, editor, memoirist, Hyun isn't exactly searching for his roots. Rather, at 70, he's trying to make sense of a life that began in the industrial city of Hamhung, near the east coast of what is now North Korea, and has somehow deposited him in New York and France."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c29bfc5b-84b7-4273-82f5-e9761f53bab0",
                                "sense_id": "0a3c31e1-9742-314e-b508-744576bfc315",
                                "text": "Hamhung is North Korea’s second city. The birthplace of the founder of Korea’s Ri dynasty and the site of a famous battle during the Korean War, Hamhung has since developed into a spacious industrial city of around 750,000 inhabitants."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "16dff87b-5950-47bd-b4b0-f404b5128256",
                                "sense_id": "0a3c31e1-9742-314e-b508-744576bfc315",
                                "text": "It was unusual for a North Korean woman of her status to get a higher education. But my mother was such a good scholar that she was accepted at a college in the nearby city of Hamhung. If given a choice, she would have liked to have become a doctor. But only students from better families are allowed a say in what they will study."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "79069977-ffe2-4a25-a061-366da6ba666e",
                                "sense_id": "0a3c31e1-9742-314e-b508-744576bfc315",
                                "text": "South Korea's Joint Chiefs of Staff said it had detected the launch of what it presumed were two ballistic missiles at about 8 a.m. (2300 GMT) from near Hamhung, on the east coast of North Korea."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
